---

## Optional: if you want to keep daisyUI

If daisyUI is required later (e.g. for a custom component), re-add `@plugin "daisyui";` and neutralize the two collisions right after the imports. Because these rules are unlayered they override daisyUI's layered output:

```css
/* Keep daisyUI but undo its collisions with the VitePress navbar */
.VPNavBarMenu.menu {
  flex-direction: row;
  flex-wrap: nowrap;
  width: auto;
  padding: 0;
}

.VPNavBar .divider {
  margin: 0;
}

.VPNavBar .divider::before,
.VPNavBar .divider::after {
  content: none;
}
```

> Note: this is a patch, not a general fix — daisyUI uses many other generic class names (`.navbar`, `.footer`, `.label`, `.link`, …) that could collide elsewhere as the docs grow. Preferring plain Tailwind utilities (as the docs already do) avoids the whole class of problems.

